From bb432be361c60beb6e9950aa738b0a89bb1d9fd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KEX patch <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] KEX: four views in a 2x2 grid, snap-out windows, built-in KEX
 suite

Four views, snap-out view windows and plugin gating for two-view
plugins. The KEX suite (PowerEditor/src/KexSuite, copied in by
kex-patch.sh) is built into notepad++.exe and gets its settings pages in
Settings > Preferences ("KEX Editing", "KEX Tabs", "KEX Windows"),
reachable from Settings > KEX Features.

Tab snapping: while a tab is dragged the core works out where it would
land (the side of a view a hidden view would open on, or another view)
and the suite draws the preview; with it on, a drop goes there instead
of showing the Move/Clone menu.

A Notepad++ for each virtual desktop: a second notepad++.exe started on
a desktop that has no Notepad++ window becomes a new Notepad++ there,
opening with a copy of the first window's tabs, carets and active tabs
(NPPM_KEX_SAVEDESKTOPCOPY / NPPM_KEX_LOADDESKTOPCOPY). Windows never
move between desktops.

A tab drag starts from anywhere on the tab once the mouse has moved the
system drag distance, and tells the suite so it can lift the tab.

The app calls itself "Notepad++ KEX" in the title bar, the About box,
the debug info and the version resource (the taskbar and Task Manager
name); the window class stays "Notepad++". Settings > KEX Features gives
way to the suite's KEX group at the end of the Settings menu, so
Notepad++'s own Settings items keep their upstream positions;
NPPM_KEX_SHOWPREFPAGE opens Preferences on a given KEX page.

